{"id": "EUVD-2026-93095", "enisaUuid": "f625dbee-b824-3960-a91e-dda22a3f9115", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsmb: client: fix server->total_read for compound encrypted PDUs\n\nIn receive_encrypted_standard(), server->total_read is left at the\nfull decrypted frame size when walking sub-PDUs of a compound encrypted\nframe. As a result, cifs_handle_standard() passes this full size\nto smb2_check_message(), causing the PDU length guards to incorrectly\nvalidate the entire compound frame instead of the current sub-PDU.\n\nThis allows truncated non-last sub-PDUs to bypass length validation,\nleading to out-of-bounds reads in smb2_get_data_area_len().\n\nFix this by setting server->total_read to the true length of the\ncurrent sub-PDU: next_cmd for non-last sub-PDUs, and the remaining\npdu_length for the last one.", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:44:12", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:14:58", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8703539d22fdbc13dd2db090ee199c3a427b8ea0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e78fc1d240b27349b45a0f1c3e3c2c401d7e230d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a46eb242e9eef3a3897d166748b23303c516e870", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ebb8a075fdc7af3d196a4f158a0e18dbc394c0e3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/282b72f9a7ef31296c48366db4128882999cc048", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f73726b83e4756fdaa099e1bc1143293bd57ad79"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98167", "GHSA-wwfg-4wrm-v6qx"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.22, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "02e4403c-e5d8-3e18-a91a-1d0c3cab98cd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "0a78f981-f61e-3ec2-9503-cdf848427d7f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b24df3e30cbf48255db866720fb71f14bf9d2f39 <ebb8a075fdc7af3d196a4f158a0e18dbc394c0e3"}, {"id": "108a7d29-3ff8-39e8-81dd-06bb50e00242", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "1e223661-0a93-3adf-a44f-a7b8b95564cd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.19"}, {"id": "3a4cd75f-4c03-3180-bb36-4b23f8846a45", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.54"}, {"id": "48eeebb7-2033-3224-a0ed-cae875ff89d7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b24df3e30cbf48255db866720fb71f14bf9d2f39 <a46eb242e9eef3a3897d166748b23303c516e870"}, {"id": "8088ca84-4950-32b2-b34d-8e881f974c8e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.189"}, {"id": "91700293-06df-30fb-9dbd-8c06b2a8bb52", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "b6e283c3-b2c4-31fa-822d-14716d2ef2e0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b24df3e30cbf48255db866720fb71f14bf9d2f39 <282b72f9a7ef31296c48366db4128882999cc048"}, {"id": "cacfb8bc-a3cb-31c3-9218-89e1224500f0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.158"}, {"id": "cb2f926a-9d45-34be-b11b-0767d19c2eef", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b24df3e30cbf48255db866720fb71f14bf9d2f39 <e78fc1d240b27349b45a0f1c3e3c2c401d7e230d"}, {"id": "d2e1ddd9-0d4c-3aa8-a887-01dc1224bb99", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b24df3e30cbf48255db866720fb71f14bf9d2f39 <8703539d22fdbc13dd2db090ee199c3a427b8ea0"}, {"id": "fe4aac0f-7e54-3f8b-a710-61ae5d1bb51f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.8"}, {"id": "ff9ca7af-3f53-30ae-abae-c5b6b04b69a4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b24df3e30cbf48255db866720fb71f14bf9d2f39 <f73726b83e4756fdaa099e1bc1143293bd57ad79"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "51cb8c2b-3261-3